ion a  seat that we took off the tories only a  few weeks ago which had added as it were  to boris johnson's uh woes and was was a  key driver in removing the prime  minister from his position so the labour  party is making electoral progress in  the ways that it matters which is actual  results that are being delivered on the  ground  i appreciate that shimano no one's  disputing the progress that's been made  it was a really low ebb when the party  was led by jeremy corbyn so to move on  from that is uh something that  definitely should have happened but i  wonder if this is a an issue of  leadership at the moment there is still  a problem isn't there with whether  labour party members people in the  shadow cabinet can go on to picket lines  can you just clear up what the decision  has been made by sakirstama as to  whether people should be on the picket  lines because we saw lisa nandi there a  couple of days ago she was reprimanded  but not sacked sanitary was set to a few  days hence before for being on a picket  line  well there's a there's a clear  difference between both of those uh  instances and so  let me just explain you know because  care has made very clear that we are a  government in waiting we want the people  of our country to put us into government  at that next election and we want that  election as soon as possible and think  it should happen as soon as the new tory  prime minister is elected a government  in waiting has to behave seriously like  a government  and be the you know model the behavior  that we would have in government if  you're a government minister you need to  be able to get around a negotiating  table with public sector unions pay  officials worker bodies representatives  and get to fair negotiations and act in  good faith you can't do that if you walk  off you know if you get to that  negotiating table by pick from picketing  at a picket line so it's been very clear  that you know labor front venture should  not be picketing a